do is also addressing ozone\npollution through state policies. For more information about\nhealth impacts and how ozone pollution forms in Colorado, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone- pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion.","ends":"2026-08-28T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Broomfield, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Adams, CO; Boulder, CO; Weld, CO; Larimer, CO; Arapahoe, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a17a27b506afd523954d57cd2deb7b4d9d4ce26d.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a17a27b506afd523954d57cd2deb7b4d9d4ce26d.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-27T23:30:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 272330 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 530 PM MDT Thu Aug 27 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Isolated/scattered high based showers/storms today and Friday with gusty winds. - Temperatures return to the 90s Friday and Saturday across the plains. - Thunderstorm coverage increases for late Saturday through Monday. && .DISCUSSION /Through Thursday/...","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-27T21:14:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Tonight and Friday... Isolated/scattered high-based showers and thunderstorms continue through early evening, with another round expected again Friday afternoon. Brief moderate to heavy rain will be possible, but the main threat will be gusty outflow winds of 30 to 40 mph. LONG TERM DISCUSSION...Friday night through Tuesday... High pressure aloft will continue to bring very warm temp","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&iss